  "scope": "The actual lambda core allocates both denominator-one records, invokes literal rational division, binary-controlled power and rational multiplication, and returns the exact original lambda raw fraction on one paid heap. Original numerator/context pointers and padded conventions are preserved. Its bound depends on original word lengths and numerical exponent value; no binary-length-only exponent claim is made. Original minimum/grid metadata preparation and complete guess/solver composition remain separate."
